  "summary": "作者区分水性动静：多吉少煞时温和适应，多煞少吉时易激动难适应。天机或贪狼的木性机智较依模式，太阳火性急智较立即行动；天同顺环境变化应对的灵活也以多吉少煞为前提，反之可能不知变通。",
  "summary_en": "The author distinguishes Water’s quiet and turbulent aspects: many benefics and few malefics favor adaptability, while the opposite favors volatility. Tian Ji or Tan Lang represents a more patterned Wood-like resourcefulness, whereas Tai Yang represents rapid Fire-like response. Tian Tong is said to adjust its response to changing circumstances, but that flexibility requires many benefics with few or no malefics; the opposite configuration may instead be inflexible.",
